WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.940
"How Much Exercise Does It Take
to Improve Aging Cognitive Function?"

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.720
Based on a meta-analysis
of 20 studies,

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.700
mental performance
may be improved

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.580
with even modest weight loss
among overweight individuals,

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.820
though that may be due
not to the weight loss per se,

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.980
but rather
the prescribed exercise.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.920
For example, one study
randomized obese elders

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.600
to one of four groups
for a year:

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.980
a weight-loss diet alone,

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.220
exercise without weight loss,
both, or neither.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.460
Compared to the control group
that did neither,

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.460
global cognition improved
in all the three other groups,

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.680
but while weight loss
and exercise

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.000
beat out weight loss alone,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.600
weight loss and exercise
didn't beat the exercise alone,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.660
suggesting that exercise is
the most potent component.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.180
The American College
of Sports Medicine

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.840
cites meta-analyses of dozens
of prospective studies

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.640
following tens of thousands
of people for years

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.320
that suggest
that those who are active

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.740
have a 38 percent lower risk
of cognitive decline

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.600
and a 39 percent lower risk

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.400
of developing
Alzheimer's disease.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.640
And, apparently,
the more, the better.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.640
Every extra 500 calories
expended a week

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.860
appears to correlate
with an additional

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.020
ten percent drop
in dementia risk.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.540
However, even light
physical activity,

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.980
such as low-intensity walking,

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:19.860
or how yoga and tai chi
are often practiced

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.720
by older adults,
has been associated

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.880
with at least
some sort of cognitive gain

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.800
in about half of the studies
done to date.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.740
If the relationship
between exercise

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.140
and dementia prevention
is cause and effect,

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.140
as much as 20 percent
of all cases

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.820
of Alzheimer's disease
in Western countries

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:38.340
may be attributable
to physical inactivity.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:41.940
That would mean more than
a million cases of Alzheimer's

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:42.900
just in the U.S. alone.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:46.500
As with all observational data,
though,

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.360
there's the potential
for confounding

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.220
or reverse causation.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.640
Maybe there's a shared factor
causing both,

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.200
such as atherosclerosis,

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.420
contributing to both inactivity
and dementia,

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.730
or maybe those
genetically predisposed

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:00.960
to exercise a lot

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.360
also have a more robust
cognitive reserve

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.820
(though a Mendelian
randomization study

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:06.780
failed to find this).

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:10.260
Instead of inactivity
leading to dementia,

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.420
dementia could lead
to inactivity.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.940
Prospective studies
following people over time

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:18.120
can show that the inactivity
does precede the dementia,

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.520
but both mental
and physical activity

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.640
can start declining
years before a diagnosis.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.980
When researchers looked closely
at the data,

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.840
only inactivity
less than 10 years

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.660
before the diagnosis
was associated with dementia,

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:34.140
suggesting the causality
may indeed be backward.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:38.100
When put to the test,
interventional trials show

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.720
physical activity
can be increased

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.680
in dementia patients,

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.660
which can improve
physical fitness,

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:46.860
but disappointingly did not
slow cognitive impairment.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.220
Perhaps, we're just not
catching people early enough?

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.860
Adults with either
normal cognition

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:54.420
or mild cognitive impairment

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.100
randomized to exercise training

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.720
tend to improve
their cognition

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:58.860
compared to those ending up

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.080
in the less active
control groups.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.580
A slight majority of studies

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.440
that concurrently tracked
brain imaging

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.300
found those randomized
to exercise

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.400
experienced a beneficial effect

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.600
on overall brain volume

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:12.060
as well as specifically
the hippocampus,

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.980
a part of the brain
that plays a critical role

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:16.860
in memory formation
and for which atrophy predicts

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.720
memory decline and dementia.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.600
The seminal study,
"Exercise training

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.060
increases size of hippocampus
and improves memory,"

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:27.180
randomized older adults
to either a year

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.760
of supervised moderate
aerobic exercise (walking)

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.700
or a control group,
which instead involved a year

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.440
of stretching
and toning classes.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.840
On average,
the hippocampus volume

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.780
of those in the control group
shrank 1.4 percent,

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.100
which is consistent

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.960
with the one to two percent
annual shrinkage

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.100
typical of old age.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.600
In contrast,

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.760
over that same year
in the walking group,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.580
their hippocampus volume
increased two percent,

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.860
which is like adding
a year or two of brain volume

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:56.160
(though may subsequently shrink
back to baseline

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.500
in as few as six weeks
of inactivity;

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.760
so you got to keep it up).

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.940
A similar study
that added a third group-

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:04.500
a resistance training arm-

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.440
found a similar
aerobic training reversal

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.600
of age-related shrinkage
in the memory centers

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.580
compared to the balance
and toning control group,

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.040
but unfortunately
there was no benefit seen

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.380
in the nonaerobic
strength-training group.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.760
It's unclear exactly which type
of exercise is best,

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.880
but the cognitive benefit
of aerobic training

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.760
appears to be larger
than resistance training.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:29.040
In most of the randomized
controlled trials

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:29.880
of older adults,

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.880
walking was the most frequently
chosen mode of exercise.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:36.600
The best volume, duration,
frequency, or intensity

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:37.800
is also unknown.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:39.720
Based on a meta-analysis

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.880
of nearly a hundred
randomized controlled trials,

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.280
more important
than session duration,

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:48.060
weekly frequency,
program duration, or intensity,

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.040
may be total training time.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:54.120
However studies spliced it up,
it appeared to take exercising

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.520
for a total
of at least 52 hours

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:59.460
before a cognitive benefit
can be established.

